# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type }})

The `portainer_endpoint_association` action de-associates an Edge environment from its agent while keeping the environment record, so another agent can associate with it.

> **Requirements:** Terraform >= 1.14 (actions). OpenTofu does not support actions; there, and with older Terraform, use the [`portainer_endpoint_association` resource](../resources/endpoint_association.md), which runs the same operation when it is created.

## Example Usage

### Run it from a lifecycle `action_trigger`

```hcl
action "portainer_endpoint_association" "edge" {
  config {
    endpoint_id = 12
  }
}

resource "terraform_data" "edge_host" {
  input = var.edge_host_serial

  lifecycle {
    action_trigger {
      events  = [before_update]
      actions = [action.portainer_endpoint_association.edge]
    }
  }
}
```

### Run it on demand

```shell
terraform apply -invoke action.portainer_endpoint_association.edge
```

## Lifecycle & Behavior

- The action runs only when it is invoked: from an `action_trigger` on the events listed there, or with `terraform apply -invoke`. A plan lists the invocations it would run; nothing is stored in state, so there is nothing to destroy and no `triggers` argument is needed to run it again.
- It sends the same requests as the `portainer_endpoint_association` resource does when it is created, with the same defaults, and fails the apply with the same errors.

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Attributes Reference

Actions have no attributes: nothing they return can be referenced elsewhere in the configuration.
